                <td headers="hd_h_rickets-xlh.T.hereditary_disorders_with_1_1_1_4" rowspan="2" valign="middle" align="left" colspan="1"><list list-type="bullet"><list-item><p>Hypophosphatemia &#x00026; hypercalciuria</p></list-item><list-item><p>Suppressed FGF23</p></list-item><list-item><p>1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D may be &#x02191;, normal, or low due to proximal tubular dysfunction.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Low molecular weight proteinuria</p></list-item></list>
